ui.glock:
🔐 <b>Group lock</b>
While the group is locked, only admins can write: the bot closes the group's permissions in Telegram and restores them when it opens.

State: {state}
Timed lock ends in: {until}
Daily auto lock: {auto}

• Timed lock: <code>Lock Group 2 h</code>
• Daily auto lock: <code>SetAutoLock 00:00 08:00</code>

ui.flood:
🌊 <b>Anti-flood</b>
If a member sends more than {count} messages within {seconds} seconds, the extra messages are deleted and the member is punished once.

State: {state}
Limit: {count} messages
Punishment: {mode}

ui.limit:
⏳ <b>Slow mode</b>
Each member may send at most {count} messages every {seconds} seconds. Messages over the quota are deleted and the member gets a short notice.

State: {state}

ui.chars:
📏 <b>Message length</b>
Messages longer than the maximum or shorter than the minimum are deleted. Useful against walls of text and one-letter spam.

Maximum length: {max}
Minimum length: {min}

ui.strict:
⚖️ <b>Strict mode</b>
Normally a locked message is only deleted. In strict mode, whoever sends one of the selected kinds is also punished.

State: {state}
Punishment: {mode}

Choose below which kinds are punished:

ui.dup:
♻️ <b>Duplicate messages</b>
A text already sent in the last {hours} hours is deleted when it is sent again. Only messages of at least {len} characters are checked, so short replies like «ok» are never affected.

State: {state}

ui.betray:
🚨 <b>Anti-betrayal</b>
If an admin bans or mutes more than {limit} members within one hour, the bot takes their rank away. Only owners can change this.

State: {state}

ui.reason:
💡 <b>Notices and reports</b>
<b>Deletion notices</b>: when a lock removes a message, the bot says why for a few seconds, so members learn the rules.
<b>Reports</b>: members reply <code>Report</code> to a bad message and the admins are alerted.

Deletion notices: {state}
Reports go to: {report}

ui.join:
🚪 <b>Joining</b>
What happens when someone joins. Open an item to set it up.

👋 Welcome: {welcome}
🚶 Goodbye: {goodbye}
🤖 Captcha: {captcha}
➕ Force add: {fadd}
📢 Force join: {fjoin}

ui.welcome:
👋 <b>Welcome</b>
Every new member gets a welcome message, optionally with a photo, GIF or video.

State: {state}
Goodbye message: {goodbye}
Welcome text: {text}
Media: {media}
Delete after: {delete}

• Text: <code>SetWelcome Hello !mention!</code> (formatting is kept)
• Media: reply to a photo or GIF with <code>SetWelcomeMedia</code>
• Goodbye text: <code>SetGoodbye …</code>
• Variables: !mention !firstname !lastname !username !userid !groupname !grouplink !grouprules !date !time !emoji

ui.fadd:
➕ <b>Force add</b>
Members must add {count} people to the group before they can write. Until then their messages are deleted with a reminder.

State: {state}
Applies to: {scope}
Completed adds expire after: {expire}

• Expiry: <code>ForceAddTime 30</code> (days) or <code>ForceAddTime off</code>
• Reminder text: <code>SetForceAddText …</code> (variables: needadd remainadd useradd)

